# Development Standards

This project was scaffolded with **TypeScript**, **AWS**, and **Jest** as the test framework. Assume these as the default context when suggesting code, tests, or architecture.

## Assumed Context (from `terraflow new`)

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Language | TypeScript |
| Runtime | Node.js |
| Target Platform | AWS |
| Test Framework | Jest |

## Project Specification

**Before making significant changes, check for `SPECIFICATION.md` in the project root.** If it exists, read it and apply its requirements. Project-specific specifications override generic standards when they conflict.

## External Standards

Follow [salte-common/standards](https://github.com/salte-common/standards) recursively. Apply as appropriate:

- **Architecture Standards** — Twelve-Factor App, modular design, testing pyramid
- **Development Standards** — Code formatting, quality, security
- **JavaScript Standards** — Language-specific guidelines
- **AWS Architecture Standards** — Platform-specific deployment and architecture
- **Deployment Standards** — IaC, CI/CD, environment config
- **Security Standards** — OWASP Top 10, data protection, API security
- **Documentation Standards** — README, API docs, code comments
- **Git Workflow Standards** — Branch strategy, tagging, release process

## When Suggesting Code

1. Use **TypeScript** conventions (runtime: **Node.js**)
2. Write tests with **Jest**
3. Target **AWS** for deployment and infrastructure
4. Reference salte-common/standards for patterns and compliance
5. Honor `SPECIFICATION.md` if present
